(borge-bug (id "BORGE-1786860090")
  (title "prod notes/tree/write-root-body stale: notes/doc/upsert empties outline kids (let* fix committed but not deployed)")
  (status closed)
  (created 2026-08-16)
  (filed-by roerick)
  (doc (|## Summary

`notes/tree/write-root-body` on the live habitat is the stale pre-fix version (parallel `let`):

  (let ((n (notes/tree/parse cur)) (b (notes/tree/body n))) ...)   ;; b refs n -> unbound: n

The `let*` fix IS committed in git (HEAD:libs/notes/lib.pp has it, with a comment: "parallel let ... threw unbound: n (broke notes/doc/upsert write path)"), but prod's deployed libs/notes/lib.pp is old, so load_library / reseed-package re-load the BUGGY code.

## Impact (data loss)

notes/tree/save-outline runs (seq (clear-headings ...) (write-root-body ...) (foldl write-heading ...)). clear-headings DELETES all kid nodes first, then write-root-body throws unbound: n — so kids are gone before the error and write-heading never runs. ANY notes/doc/upsert on a note that has kids empties it.

Reproduced: the live agents note (slug agents) was emptied to ["root","Agents (living AGENTS.md)","","",[]] this session (93 nodes -> 0). Restored from a captured copy via the clear-headings + write-heading bypass (skipping write-root-body).

This ALSO breaks the new /issues workflow end-to-end: notes/issues/add -> notes/doc/upsert -> same bug. Browser /issues, scripts/file-issue.sh, and (notes/issues/add ...) all destroy existing log/issues entries then error on current prod.

## Why reseed didn't fix it

reseed_package sets seed_additive <- false (clobber) and calls load_library, which reads from the filesystem (PP_LIBS_DIR / libs/<pkg>/lib.pp, image/lib/loader.ml). Prod's file is stale, so reseed re-writes the buggy version. (define) after load_library fixes the live env for that call only; the next load_library clobbers it back. (unbind) is refused on system/main (and define is no-op against an existing inherited binding within the same call as load_library).

## Fix (needs server access / redeploy)

1. Update prod's libs/notes/lib.pp from git HEAD (deploy / git pull).
2. Restart the image (so boot load_library picks up the fixed file).
3. (reseed-package "notes") on system/main to refresh stored defs.
4. Verify: (function-source "notes/tree/write-root-body

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------
;; RESOLUTION 2026-09-27
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------
;; Both parts of this bug are resolved.
;;
;; (1) THE TRIGGER (write-root-body throwing unbound: n from a parallel
;;     let) was fixed in git by 8622096 on 2026-08-15 and IS deployed:
;;     prod's bound notes/tree/write-root-body reads
;;       (let* ((n (notes/tree/parse cur)) (b (notes/tree/body n))) ...)
;;     and /usr/local/libexec/pricklypear/current/libs/notes/lib.pp carries
;;     the let* forms. reseed-package no longer reloads the buggy code,
;;     because the RELEASE file it reads is no longer stale.
;;
;; (2) THE DESTRUCTIVE ORDERING this report also identified
;;     (\"notes/tree/save-outline runs (seq (clear-headings ...)
;;      (write-root-body ...) ...). clear-headings DELETES all kid nodes
;;      first ... so kids are gone before the error\") was NOT fixed in
;;     August — only the trigger was. Nine weeks later the SAME note was
;;     emptied again by the SAME ordering, with a different trigger (the
;;     alist body-boundary rejection, BORGE-1790535211). save-outline is
;;     now write-then-sweep AND atomic (b4337b5), so a failure in the write
;;     half leaves the previous outline intact instead of an empty note.
;;     See BORGE-1790546246 for what remains.
;;
;; CLOSED on (1) since that was this bug's stated subject and it is
;; verifiably fixed and deployed; (2) is closed by b4337b5 and its
;; remainder is tracked in BORGE-1790546246.
;;
;; LESSON (worth carrying into future triage): this report named a
;; destructive STRUCTURE alongside its immediate trigger. Fixing the
;; trigger closed the repro without closing the hazard, and because the
;; ordering half was never split out into its own issue, nothing recorded
;; that a note-destroying sequence was still live. When a report contains a
;; delete-then-do shape, split the STRUCTURE into its own issue at
;; triage time; do not let a fixed trigger imply the structure is safe.
") shows let*; notes/doc/upsert on a test note preserves kids.

After this, /issues works and the agents note is safe to edit again.

## Caveat until redeploy

The restored agents note is durable as long as nothing calls notes/doc/upsert on it (e.g. outline-UI set-body, /issues-style add). Any such edit will re-empty it until the fix is deployed.|))
)
